													<CONFIG-VARIANT>VARIANT-PRE-COMPILE</CONFIG-VARIANT>
												</ECUC-VALUE-CONFIGURATION-CLASS>
												<ECUC-VALUE-CONFIGURATION-CLASS>
													<CONFIG-CLASS>PRE-COMPILE</CONFIG-CLASS>
													<CONFIG-VARIANT>VARIANT-LINK-TIME</CONFIG-VARIANT>
												</ECUC-VALUE-CONFIGURATION-CLASS>
											</VALUE-CONFIG-CLASSES>
											<SYMBOLIC-NAME-VALUE>false</SYMBOLIC-NAME-VALUE>
											<DEFAULT-VALUE>false</DEFAULT-VALUE>
										</ECUC-BOOLEAN-PARAM-DEF>
										<ECUC-BOOLEAN-PARAM-DEF UUID="22e2cce4-9528-405b-8d2b-584e602ace9d">
											<SHORT-NAME>FeeReportExceptions</SHORT-NAME>
											<DESC>
												<L-2 L="EN">Enables the reporting of critical errors via callback. (Detection is always enabled, independent from the setting here).
When enabled and a critical error is detected, the callback void Fee_30_FlexNor_DiagnosticHandler_UserCallback(EventPublishedInfoType eventInfo) (name not configurable) will be called by the Fee.
The integrator must implement the callback. The given parameter eventInfo will give some more information about the exception.
It is highly recommended to keep this option enabled.

Background:
It is mandatory that the integrator and the hardware platform fullfil some requirements, that can be found in the Technical Reference (see chapter "Diagnostic Handler").
If these requirements are not met, the Fee is not able to work properly.
So the integrator is in charge to assure, that every single requirement is met.

However, if one requirement is not met, the effect will not be detectable immediately.
Hence, it is quite difficult to recognize wrong integrations. Usually, they are recognized when it is already to late.

In order to support the integrator, the Fee tries to detect unexpected effects which are usually caused by integration errors and can lead to data loss or unexpected behavior.
In this case the Fee raises an exception.

It is very important, that the source of the exception, i.e. the wrong integration, is fixed. When the FeeExceptionReporting mechanism is enabled, the Fee will notify the integrator in case an exception was detected.
Depending on the error code, the integrator/tester can then get more information, what must be fixed. It is highly recommended to keep this setting enabled.</L-2>
											</DESC>
											<LOWER-MULTIPLICITY>1</LOWER-MULTIPLICITY>
											<UPPER-MULTIPLICITY>1</UPPER-MULTIPLICITY>
											<SCOPE>LOCAL</SCOPE>
											<MULTIPLICITY-CONFIG-CLASSES>
												<ECUC-MULTIPLICITY-CONFIGURATION-CLASS>
													<CONFIG-CLASS>PRE-COMPILE</CONFIG-CLASS>
													<CONFIG-VARIANT>VARIANT-PRE-COMPILE</CONFIG-VARIANT>
												</ECUC-MULTIPLICITY-CONFIGURATION-CLASS>
												<ECUC-MULTIPLICITY-CONFIGURATION-CLASS>
													<CONFIG-CLASS>PRE-COMPILE</CONFIG-CLASS>
													<CONFIG-VARIANT>VARIANT-LINK-TIME</CONFIG-VARIANT>
												</ECUC-MULTIPLICITY-CONFIGURATION-CLASS>
											</MULTIPLICITY-CONFIG-CLASSES>
											<ORIGIN>Vector Informatik</ORIGIN>
											<POST-BUILD-VARIANT-MULTIPLICITY>false</POST-BUILD-VARIANT-MULTIPLICITY>
											<POST-BUILD-VARIANT-VALUE>false</POST-BUILD-VARIANT-VALUE>
											<REQUIRES-INDEX>false</REQUIRES-INDEX>
											<VALUE-CONFIG-CLASSES>
												<ECUC-VALUE-CONFIGURATION-CLASS>
													<CONFIG-CLASS>PRE-COMPILE</CONFIG-CLASS>
													<CONFIG-VARIANT>VARIANT-PRE-COMPILE</CONFIG-VARIANT>
												</ECUC-VALUE-CONFIGURATION-CLASS>
												<ECUC-VALUE-CONFIGURATION-CLASS>
													<CONFIG-CLASS>PRE-COMPILE</CONFIG-CLASS>
													<CONFIG-VARIANT>VARIANT-LINK-TIME</CONFIG-VARIANT>
												</ECUC-VALUE-CONFIGURATION-CLASS>
											</VALUE-CONFIG-CLASSES>
											<SYMBOLIC-NAME-VALUE>false</SYMBOLIC-NAME-VALUE>
											<DEFAULT-VALUE>true</DEFAULT-VALUE>
										</ECUC-BOOLEAN-PARAM-DEF>
										<ECUC-BOOLEAN-PARAM-DEF UUID="5641da17-2b0a-4928-a8cb-c60d90174028">
											<SHORT-NAME>FeeReportDebugNotifications</SHORT-NAME>
											<DESC>
												<L-2 L="EN">Enables the reporting of debug notifications via callback. FeeReportExceptions must be enabled, to be able to enable the reporting of debug notifications.
When enabled and a job "milestone" is reached, the callback void Fee_30_FlexNor_DiagnosticHandler_UserCallback(EventPublishedInfoType eventInfo) (name not configurable) will be called by Fee.

Such a milestone can be the single write steps (e.g. writing the chunk commit marker) or other operations (e.g. start of a space garbage collection...)
This allows the integrator/tester to get some kind of a log, when something is not working as expected. This log will also help the Vector support to give better and faster feedback.
It is recommended to keep this option disabled and enable it, when a debug scenario occurs</L-2>
											</DESC>
											<LOWER-MULTIPLICITY>1</LOWER-MULTIPLICITY>
											<UPPER-MULTIPLICITY>1</UPPER-MULTIPLICITY>
											<SCOPE>LOCAL</SCOPE>
											<MULTIPLICITY-CONFIG-CLASSES>
												<ECUC-MULTIPLICITY-CONFIGURATION-CLASS>
													<CONFIG-CLASS>PRE-COMPILE</CONFIG-CLASS>
													<CONFIG-VARIANT>VARIANT-PRE-COMPILE</CONFIG-VARIANT>
												</ECUC-MULTIPLICITY-CONFIGURATION-CLASS>
												<ECUC-MULTIPLICITY-CONFIGURATION-CLASS>
													<CONFIG-CLASS>PRE-COMPILE</CONFIG-CLASS>
													<CONFIG-VARIANT>VARIANT-LINK-TIME</CONFIG-VARIANT>
												</ECUC-MULTIPLICITY-CONFIGURATION-CLASS>
											</MULTIPLICITY-CONFIG-CLASSES>
											<ORIGIN>Vector Informatik</ORIGIN>
											<POST-BUILD-VARIANT-MULTIPLICITY>false</POST-BUILD-VARIANT-MULTIPLICITY>
											<POST-BUILD-VARIANT-VALUE>false</POST-BUILD-VARIANT-VALUE>
											<REQUIRES-INDEX>false</REQUIRES-INDEX>
											<VALUE-CONFIG-CLASSES>
												<ECUC-VALUE-CONFIGURATION-CLASS>
													<CONFIG-CLASS>PRE-COMPILE</CONFIG-CLASS>
													<CONFIG-VARIANT>VARIANT-PRE-COMPILE</CONFIG-VARIANT>
												</ECUC-VALUE-CONFIGURATION-CLASS>
												<ECUC-VALUE-CONFIGURATION-CLASS>
													<CONFIG-CLASS>PRE-COMPILE</CONFIG-CLASS>
													<CONFIG-VARIANT>VARIANT-LINK-TIME</CONFIG-VARIANT>
												</ECUC-VALUE-CONFIGURATION-CLASS>
											</VALUE-CONFIG-CLASSES>
											<SYMBOLIC-NAME-VALUE>false</SYMBOLIC-NAME-VALUE>
											<DEFAULT-VALUE>false</DEFAULT-VALUE>
										</ECUC-BOOLEAN-PARAM-DEF>
									</PARAMETERS>
									<REFERENCES>
